    <div class="ind-q">
      The industry has been<br>
treating the symptom,<br>
<em>never the real problem.</em>
    </div>
  

  <div class="ind-right">
    
      <p class="ind-label">Why the category keeps failing</p>
    

    
      <p class="ind-p">A spot treatment clears the breakout before the barrier rebuilds. A hydration serum deposits moisture without activating the skin's own production. A brightening product suppresses melanin without addressing why it's being overproduced. Each product solves for the visible sign. None of them address the underlying biology that produced it.</p>
    

    
      <p class="ind-p">The result is a maintenance loop. The products work while you use them. The moment you stop, the original condition returns. Not because your skin is broken. Because nothing was ever rebuilt.</p>
    

    
      <p class="ind-close">The real problem was never the spot or the dryness. It was the skin's own ability to repair itself, and nobody was rebuilding that.</p>
    
  </div>
</section>

